          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-amber-400\">🦴 1. What is Human Evolution?</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Definition:</strong> Human evolution is the long-term biological and cultural development of humans from earlier hominin ancestors.<br>\n                  • <strong>Scientific Evidence:</strong> Fossilized skeletal bones, preserved footprints (e.g. Laetoli), stone tools (Oldowan, Acheulean), and archaeological habitation sites.<br>\n                  • <strong>Key Milestones:</strong> Development of upright bipedal walking (walking on two legs), expansion of cranial (brain) capacity, precision grip, tool manufacturing, and symbolic language.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400\">🇪🇹 2. Ethiopia: Cradle of Humankind</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Lucy (Dinknesh):</strong> In 1974, a 3.2-million-year-old fossil of <em>Australopithecus afarensis</em> (40% complete skeleton) was discovered at Hadar in the <strong>Afar region of Ethiopia</strong>. Lucy proved that upright walking (bipedalism) preceded large brain development.<br>\n                  • <strong>Ardipithecus ramidus (Ardi):</strong> Discovered in the Middle Awash of Afar, dating to 4.4 million years ago.<br>\n                  • <strong>Homo sapiens idaltu:</strong> Discovered at Herto (Afar), dating to ~160,000 years ago, representing early anatomically modern humans.<br>\n                  • <strong>Learned Culture:</strong> Unlike physical traits inherited through biological DNA, <strong>culture is learned</strong> through social transmission, tool making, language, and cooperation.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
