          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-amber-400\">🚗 1. Definition and Modes of Transportation</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Definition:</strong> Transportation is the movement of people, animals, and goods from one place to another.<br>\n                  • <strong>Four Major Modes:</strong><br>\n                  - <strong>Road Transport:</strong> Most flexible; provides door-to-door delivery; vital for local trade and rural access.<br>\n                  - <strong>Railway Transport:</strong> Cost-effective for moving heavy, bulky freight and large numbers of passengers over long overland distances (e.g., Addis Ababa-Djibouti electrified railway).<br>\n                  - <strong>Water Transport:</strong> Most economical mode for bulk international trade across oceans, seas, and navigable lakes/rivers.<br>\n                  - <strong>Air Transport:</strong> Fastest mode; ideal for perishable goods and urgent long-distance passenger travel (e.g., Ethiopian Airlines).\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-cyan-400\">📈 2. Economic and Social Impact</h4>\n                <div class=\"space-y-1 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300\">\n                  <p>• <strong>Market Linkages:</strong> Connects agricultural producers in rural Ethiopia with urban consumers and export markets.</p>\n                  <p>• <strong>Access to Social Services:</strong> Enables citizens to reach referral hospitals, secondary schools, universities, and administrative centers.</p>\n                  <p>• <strong>Challenges of Inadequate Transport:</strong> High transportation costs, prolonged travel times, post-harvest crop spoilage, and economic isolation of remote communities.</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
