          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-amber-400\">🚶 1. Population Movements and Cultural Integration</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Underlying Drivers:</strong> Search for grazing pastures and arable land, demographic growth, prolonged regional droughts, trade expansion, and geopolitical conflicts.<br>\n                  • <strong>Transformative Outcomes:</strong> The 16th-century Oromo population movement spread communities across southern, central, eastern, and western Ethiopia. This facilitated deep cultural intermingling, intermarriage, linguistic borrowing, adoption of shared farming techniques, and socio-political alliances.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-emerald-400\">🗳️ 2. The Gadaa Governance System</h4>\n                <p class=\"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed\">\n                  • <strong>Definition:</strong> <strong>Gadaa</strong> is an indigenous egalitarian democratic system of socio-political governance and social organization developed by the Oromo people.<br>\n                  • <strong>Core Organizational Features:</strong><br>\n                  - <em>Age-Grade Cycles:</em> Males pass through successive generational classes every <strong>8 years</strong> (Dabballee, Foollee, Qondaala, etc.), with each grade assigning specific social, military, and administrative responsibilities.<br>\n                  - <em>The Gadaa Class:</em> The governing class assumes executive power for a single fixed 8-year term under the elected <strong>Abba Gadaa</strong> (spokesman/leader).<br>\n                  - <em>Democratic Checks and Peaceful Transition:</em> Power is handed over peacefully at the Chafe (general assembly) with strict accountability, term limits, consensus decision-making, and conflict resolution (Jaarsummaa). Inscribed by UNESCO as Intangible Cultural Heritage.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
