          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-amber-400\">📋 Official High-Yield Differences Table</h4>\n                <div class=\"overflow-x-auto text-xs text-slate-300\">\n                  <table class=\"w-full text-left border-collapse\">\n                    <thead>\n                      <tr class=\"border-b border-slate-800 text-cyan-400\">\n                        <th class=\"p-2\">Comparative Pair</th>\n                        <th class=\"p-2\">Official Textbook Distinction</th>\n                      </tr>\n                    </thead>\n                    <tbody class=\"divide-y divide-slate-850\">\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Rotation vs Revolution</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Rotation:</strong> Earth spins on axis (~24h), causing day/night.<br><strong>Revolution:</strong> Earth orbits the Sun (~365¼d), with 23.5° tilt causing seasons.</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Magma vs Lava</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Magma:</strong> Molten rock beneath Earth’s surface.<br><strong>Lava:</strong> Magma that breaks through and reaches Earth’s surface.</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Igneous / Sedimentary / Metamorphic</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Igneous:</strong> Cooling and solidification of molten rock.<br><strong>Sedimentary:</strong> Compaction/cementation of deposited sediments.<br><strong>Metamorphic:</strong> Alteration of existing rock by heat, pressure, and fluids without melting.</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Population vs Density</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Population:</strong> Total number of people living in a place.<br><strong>Density:</strong> Number of people per unit of land area (people/km²).</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Over / Under / Optimal Population</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Over:</strong> Population large relative to resources, creating pressure.<br><strong>Under:</strong> Too few people to use resources effectively.<br><strong>Optimal:</strong> Size suitably balanced with resources and technology.</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Renewable vs Non-renewable</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Renewable:</strong> Naturally replenished over a short human timescale.<br><strong>Non-renewable:</strong> Finite on a human timescale (takes millions of years).</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Immigration vs Emigration</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Immigration:</strong> Moving INTO a country or place.<br><strong>Emigration:</strong> Moving OUT OF a country or place.</td>\n                      </tr>\n                      <tr>\n                        <td class=\"p-2 font-bold text-slate-200\">Ancient vs Medieval</td>\n                        <td class=\"p-2\"><strong>Ancient:</strong> Earliest civilizations up to the classical fall of Rome.<br><strong>Medieval:</strong> Period between ancient civilizations and the early modern era.</td>\n                      </tr>\n                    </tbody>\n                  </table>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
