          "coreNotes": "\n            <div class=\"space-y-4 text-slate-200\">\n              <div class=\"p-4 rounded-xl bg-space-900 border border-slate-800 space-y-2\">\n                <h4 class=\"text-sm font-bold text-amber-400\">📖 Official CBA Short-Answer Key (Questions 11 - 30)</h4>\n                <div class=\"space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300\">\n                  <p><strong>11. Two pieces of evidence Earth is approximately spherical:</strong> Curved horizon; circular shadow during lunar eclipses; ships disappearing hull-first over the horizon (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>12. Four Earth spheres:</strong> Lithosphere, atmosphere, hydrosphere, biosphere.</p>\n                  <p><strong>13. Magma vs lava:</strong> Magma is molten rock below the surface; lava is molten rock at the surface.</p>\n                  <p><strong>14. Three major rock types:</strong> Igneous, sedimentary, metamorphic.</p>\n                  <p><strong>15. Two reasons population is unevenly distributed:</strong> Climate, water availability, relief, soils, jobs, transport, history (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>16. What is human evolution?</strong> The long-term biological and cultural development of humans from earlier hominin ancestors.</p>\n                  <p><strong>17. Two benefits of transportation:</strong> Connects markets; moves people and goods; improves access to services; supports regional development (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>18. Define natural resource:</strong> A useful material or condition provided by nature.</p>\n                  <p><strong>19. Two causes of environmental degradation:</strong> Deforestation, overgrazing, pollution, soil erosion, mining, urban expansion (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>20. Explain optimal population:</strong> A population size that is suitable and balanced relative to available resources, technology, and economic conditions.</p>\n                  <p><strong>21. Two ancient civilizations of the world:</strong> Mesopotamia, Egypt, Indus Valley, China, Greece, Rome (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>22. Two contributions of ancient Egypt:</strong> Writing (hieroglyphics), monumental architecture (pyramids), mathematics, medicine, administration, irrigation agriculture (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>23. Two ancient African kingdoms/states:</strong> Egypt, Nubia/Kush, Meroë (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>24. Two characteristics of Aksum:</strong> Red Sea trade, minted coinage, monumental stelae, adoption of Christianity, organized state administration (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>25. Importance of trade routes to states:</strong> Connected regions, moved goods and people, supported commercial exchange, and provided tax revenues for state functions.</p>\n                  <p><strong>26. What is demographic overload?</strong> When population pressure exceeds the capacity of available resources, services, and infrastructure.</p>\n                  <p><strong>27. Two effects of terrorism:</strong> Loss of life/injury, pervasive fear, forced displacement, economic disruption, damage to institutions (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>28. Two ways to reduce human trafficking:</strong> Public awareness, safe migration information, strong law enforcement, victim protection, reducing economic vulnerability (any two).</p>\n                  <p><strong>29. Differentiate immigration and emigration:</strong> Immigration is moving into a place or country; emigration is moving out of a place or country.</p>\n                  <p><strong>30. Why is sustainable resource use important?</strong> It meets present human needs while protecting resources and environmental quality for future generations.</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          ",
